      "side": 1,
      "message": "This might not be needed, because the `false` at [2] means that if the pipeline layout changes, EVERYTHING is invalidated. (in retrospect that move of the logic in the frontend is more confusing than anything) so there might be a way to avoid the need to track that. That said, here we don\u0027t get called when the pipeline layout changes, so we don\u0027t know that the resource table binding should be invalidated (it would be here https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/dawn/src/dawn/native/BindGroupTracker.h;drc\u003d1d1fcea6ebbc1c2c3d04ab5538c74f742c66444f;l\u003d111)\n\nI think right now there might be a bug if we change between two root signatures that use the resource table, ah no it doesn\u0027t happen because at [3] we apply the resource table all the time.",
      "revId": "ae3a6f19ed282cb3853393436270d1770651da81",
